  "recommendation": "CONDITIONAL HOLD: mixed workload met the five-second p95 target in both controlled fixtures, but two of 18 concurrent reads at 1,000 rows returned bounded 503. Complete notification integration and passing deployment-equivalent capacity evidence remain prerequisites.",
  "rootCause": "Private-list transactions read the owner and organization before writing an authorization fence. Same-owner status writes incremented the same User document, causing snapshot conflicts and repeated identity validation. The path had no single end-to-end deadline, so per-command limits did not bound cumulative retry latency.",
  "selectedFix": {
    "summary": "The private application workflow now starts one monotonic 5,000 ms budget at the controller, makes the existing owner fence the first transaction operation, retains organization/settings/job/application fences, and uses a 64-attempt cap with bounded jitter before callback retries.",
    "driver": "Cursor reads share the transaction timeout context so multibatch reads use the same deadline and getMore does not receive an invalid maxTimeMS.",
    "security": "Canonical SHA-256 identity verification, consent, exact totals, 10,000-row capacity, batch size, live owner/organization/membership/session checks, snapshot reads and lifecycle CAS are retained.",
    "uncertainCommit": "The driver retries unknown commit results. The application callback is not replayed for an uncertain commit; mutation timeout/unknown commit returns explicit HTTP 503 unconfirmed outcome and requires status refresh.",
    "scope": "Workflow-specific. Other workflows and notification transaction defaults retain existing behavior."
  },
